 	SETTING("experimental.busy_wait_reference", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Busy wait reference duration", "The emulator's short active waits (before a thread yields its core or sleeps) are written in ticks of the system counter. On a device whose counter runs faster than the 24 MHz of the reference iPhones they lasted proportionally less (42 times less on a 1 GHz counter). Automatic keeps the reference duration on every device. Disabled restores the previous duration. No effect with SPU Spin Timing = Calibrated. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.busy_wait_reference, 0, 0, 0),
 	SETTING("experimental.lever_comparison", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Lever comparison between report windows", "Diagnostic, for a measurement asked for on purpose. Enabled: during the first minutes of a game the performance report turns Writer lock park spin and Busy wait reference duration (each only while its own setting is Automatic) off and on again between its 5 second windows, in three passes of 80 seconds, then leaves both on; every switch is written to the performance journal, and the frame rate can vary between windows during a pass. Automatic and Disabled never alternate: both levers stay as their own settings say. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.lever_comparison, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.event_waits_when_hot", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Event waits when hot", "Once the iPhone reports a serious thermal state, three short waits of the emulator (a write lock waiting for the PPU threads to stop, a PPU thread waiting for that lock, the RSX waiting for new commands) sleep the CPU core until the awaited write instead of spinning on it. They wait for the same thing, for the same time at most. Automatic: from the serious thermal state. Enabled: always. Disabled: never, the previous waits. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.event_waits_when_hot, 0, 0, 0),
 	GAME_SETTING("experimental.put_epoch_horizon", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Texture epoch at the PUT horizon", "With Texture Validation Per FIFO Batch, every new batch of guest commands the RSX noticed made every texture check its contents again, even while the RSX was still executing commands published earlier. The recheck now starts when the RSX reaches the first command that was not yet published at the previous one; semaphores, RSX writes and the end of a frame recheck as before. Every texture is still checked before any command published after its last check uses it. Automatic enables it for God of War III; Disabled rechecks at every batch noticed, as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.put_epoch_horizon, 0, 0, 0),
 	GAME_SETTING("experimental.heavy_putllc_trace", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Heavy PUTLLC trace on resume", "Diagnostic. When the game leaves a pause (in-game menu closed), records for each SPU thread up to 512 consecutive PUTLLC that change data (address, changed part, values read, asked and found) and writes them to the performance journal; two captures per boot at most. Nothing in the reservation protocol changes. Automatic and Disabled leave it off. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.heavy_putllc_trace, 0, 0, 0),
 	GAME_SETTING("experimental.ppu_region_profile", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "PPU region profile on resume", "Diagnostic. When the game leaves a pause (in-game menu closed), samples the PPU threads about once per millisecond for at most 5 seconds and writes the busiest code regions of the running ones to the performance journal; three captures per boot at most. The position sampled is the last return, indirect call, system call or reservation instruction, not the exact instruction. Automatic and Disabled leave it off. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.ppu_region_profile, 0, 0, 0),
